### Git metadata ###
# Git history, hooks, and attributes — never needed at image build/run time, only bloats the
# build context. Keeping them out also avoids leaking commit info into images.

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

### Claude Code ###
# Session state, settings, todos, and project notes have no place in a production image and
# may contain references to local paths or workflow details we don't want shipped.

.claude/
CLAUDE.md

### This file ###
# The build-context filter list shouldn't be inside the image itself.

.dockerignore

### Documentation ###
# Markdown docs, the docs/ tree, and the license aren't needed at runtime. (License obligations
# are usually met via image labels / OCI annotations, not by shipping the LICENSE file.)

*.md
docs/
LICENSE

### IDE / editor state ###
# Per-developer machine state — non-reproducible and irrelevant to the running container.

.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache

### OS junk ###
# Thumbnail caches, Finder metadata, and editor swap/backup files leak from host filesystems.

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo

### Build outputs ###
# Local compile artifacts — the image's RUN steps should produce their own from clean source.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
dist/
build/

### Node ###
# Dependency trees and tool logs — `npm/yarn install` inside the image, never copy from host
# (host node_modules can contain platform-specific native modules that break in-container).

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tgz

### Python ###
# Bytecode, type-checker caches, and virtualenvs — recreate inside the image to avoid
# host-Python-version contamination.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

### CI / VCS hosting metadata ###
# Workflow definitions belong in the repo for CI, not in the runtime image.

.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml
.circleci/

### Balena CLI workspace + saved images ###
# Generated locally by balena tooling. Including saved tarballs in the build context can
# balloon image size and creates near-recursive build inputs.

.balena/
*.tar
*.tar.gz

### Local docker-compose overrides ###
# Compose files aren't parsed during `docker build`, but keep them out so they can't be
# accidentally COPY'd in by a broad `COPY . .` step.

docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

### Logs / temp / backups ###
# Stale runtime artifacts and editor backups have no place in a fresh build context.

logs/
*.log
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak

### Test results / coverage ###
# Output of test runs — regenerated on every CI run, never shipped to production.

coverage/
**/TestResults/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
htmlcov/

### Secrets — NEVER ship these into an image ###
# Env files, keys, certs, and credential blobs. Anything baked into an image is recoverable
# by anyone who pulls it. `.env.example` is the only template safe to include.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.crt
credentials.json
secrets.json
secrets/
ssh-keys/
